@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Desktop capture readiness and retry states
state "Open collector" as Open {
  state "Ready\nno unfinished capture" as Ready
  state "Recording" as Recording
  state "Retry stop / close" as StopRetry
  state "Captured samples" as Captured
  state "Retry WAV publication" as WriteRetry
  Captured : entry / attempt atomic WAV publication
  [*] --> Ready
  Ready --> Recording : Record [start succeeds]
  Ready --> Ready : start fails [stream closed] / report
  Ready --> StopRetry : start cleanup fails / retain handle
  Recording --> StopRetry : stop fails (device or concatenation)
  Recording --> StopRetry : Close [cleanup fails] / report; keep window
  Recording --> Captured : stop succeeds [samples exist]
  Recording --> Ready : stop succeeds [no samples] / keep prior attachment
  StopRetry --> StopRetry : retry fails / retain retry state
  StopRetry --> Captured : retry succeeds [samples exist]
  StopRetry --> Ready : retry succeeds [no samples]
  Captured --> Ready : publication succeeds / stage generated filename
  Captured --> WriteRetry : publication fails / retain array
  WriteRetry --> Captured : Retry audio save
  StopRetry --> Ready : Clear [cleanup succeeds] / discard draft audio
  WriteRetry --> Ready : Clear [cleanup succeeds] / discard array and draft audio
  Ready --> Ready : attach, save, Clear [operation succeeds] / update ownership
}
Open --> [*] : Close [confirmed if needed; cleanup succeeds]
note right of Recording
  Saving, attaching and playback
  are disabled while capture is unfinished.
  Clear is disabled during live recording.
end note
legend bottom
  Conceptual states derive from recording, stream, pending-stop and captured-array fields.
  Ready may contain a staged filename; it does not mean an empty form.
  Failed cleanup keeps the window/retry state available, not a false closed status.
  Draft-owned files may be discarded; committed recordings are never owned by the draft.
endlegend
@enduml
